Port to fvwm 2.7: ButtonStyle FullPixmap -> Pixmap ... -- Flat, WindowFont
-> Style * Font, new MenuStyle syntax, EdgeResistance with one argument
plus EdgeMove* styles, TitleStyle flags after "--". Fonts get a fixed
pixel size (TNLFont), since *helvetica*bold-r*12* now also matches the
17 pixel 100dpi fonts, and the title bar is FONT_SIZE+6 pixels high to
fit the 18 pixel title button pixmaps, as in fvwm 2.0.

diff --git a/.fvwm2rc.defines b/.fvwm2rc.defines
index 386592e..a71ee96 100644
--- a/.fvwm2rc.defines
+++ b/.fvwm2rc.defines
@@ -148,16 +148,18 @@ define(`MINI_ICONS')
 
 # Uncomment this if you want to use Win95-like buttons
 # you don't need to uncomment this if you're using Fvwm95
-# I'd suggest switching TITLE_STYLE to `LeftJustified Flat' if you use
+# I'd suggest switching TITLE_STYLE to `LeftJustified -- Flat' if you use
 # WIN95_BUTTONS, as they themselves are flat
 #define(`WIN95_BUTTONS')
 
 # TITLE_STYLE should be a {justification,appearance} pair from fvwm's TitleStyle option
 # justification is one of Centered, RightJustified, or LeftJustified
-# appearance is one of Raised, Sunk, or Flat
+# appearance is one of Raised, Sunk, or Flat, after "--" (fvwm 2.2 and later)
 # This does nothing in Fvwm95
-# eg. `Centered Flat'
-define(`TITLE_STYLE',`LeftJustified Raised')
+# eg. `Centered -- Flat'
+# The title bar height can be set with TITLE_HEIGHT (default FONT_SIZE+6,
+# which fits the 18 pixel title buttons)
+define(`TITLE_STYLE',`LeftJustified -- Raised')
 
 # Uncomment this to use pixmap buttons, instead of button style drawings.
 # The advantage of pixmap buttons is that they always stay in the multi-tone dark grey.
